  "description": "<img width=\"25%\" src=\"https://gtif-ukif.github.io/gtif-ukif-client/assets/ucl-logo.webp\">\n\nDrought can sometimes be manifested by reduction in water reservoir extents. Explore the RGB albedo for 2022 for UK+Ireland by switching the Inland water body mask on and off and try a similar operation for FR for Aug25 using the ESA WC21 water body mask. Very few reservoirs had a detectable change in extent in the August drought month such as Ardingley, Sussex, UK at 51.084ºN, -0.102ºW and Bewl Water at 51.074ºN, 0.394ºE.",
